.TH DMRCRACK 1 "May 2026" "FSP\-Labs" "dmrcrack Manual"
.SH NAME
dmrcrack \- GPU\-accelerated RC4 40\-bit key recovery for DMR Enhanced Privacy
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dmrcrack
.B \-\-bin
.I payload.bin
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dmrcrack
brute\-forces the 5\-byte (40\-bit) RC4 key used in DMR Enhanced Privacy
encrypted voice transmissions.
It takes demodulated voice frame payloads in
.I .bin
format (produced by DSD\-FME with
.B \-Q
DSP output mode) and exhaustively searches the 40\-bit keyspace
(up to 1,099,511,627,775 candidates).
.PP
When an NVIDIA CUDA\-capable GPU is available, the search is offloaded to the
GPU with a configurable CPU assist.
If no compatible GPU is detected,
.B dmrcrack
falls back to a multi\-threaded CPU search automatically.
.PP
Progress is periodically saved to a
.I .progress
checkpoint file so an interrupted search can be resumed without restarting
from the beginning.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-bin " file"
.I .bin
payload file to search against.
Required.
The file must contain at least one line in the format produced by
.BR dsdfme_dsp_to_bin.py :
66 hex characters (33 bytes) optionally followed by
.I ;ALG=XX;KID=XX;MI=XXXXXXXX
metadata.
.TP
.BI \-\-start " hex"
Start of the key search range.
40\-bit hexadecimal value (10 hex digits).
Default:
.B 0000000000
.TP
.BI \-\-end " hex"
End of the key search range (inclusive).
40\-bit hexadecimal value.
Default:
.B FFFFFFFFFF
.TP
.BI \-\-threads " n"
Number of CPU worker threads.
Default: number of logical CPUs minus one.
.TP
.BI \-\-gpu\-pct " 50\-95"
Percentage of the keyspace assigned to the GPU when CUDA is available.
The remaining fraction is searched in parallel by CPU workers.
Default:
.B 80
.TP
.BI \-\-samples " n"
Number of payload lines sampled per key candidate.
0 (default) means all lines.
Reducing this speeds up the search at the cost of accuracy.
.TP
.BI \-\-key " hex"
Score a single specific key and exit, without running the full search.
Useful for validating that a candidate key is correct.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-resume
Ignore any existing checkpoint file and start the search from the beginning.
.TP
.B \-\-help ", " \-h
Print a usage summary and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success (search completed, or
.B \-\-help
was requested).
.TP
.B 1
Error (missing arguments, unreadable payload file, engine failure).
.SH FILES
.TP
.IB payload.bin .progress
Checkpoint file written periodically during a search, in the same directory
as the payload file.
Contains the last tested key so the search can be resumed.
Deleted automatically when the search completes successfully.
.SH EXAMPLES
Full keyspace search using a captured payload:
.PP
.RS
.EX
dmrcrack \-\-bin capture.bin
.EE
.RE
.PP
Resume an interrupted search:
.PP
.RS
.EX
dmrcrack \-\-bin capture.bin
.EE
.RE
(Checkpoint is loaded automatically if
.I capture.bin.progress
exists.)
.PP
Score a known candidate key:
.PP
.RS
.EX
dmrcrack \-\-bin capture.bin \-\-key AB12CD34EF
.EE
.RE
.PP
Search a subrange on 8 CPU threads with no GPU:
.PP
.RS
.EX
dmrcrack \-\-bin capture.bin \-\-start 0000000000 \-\-end 000FFFFFFF \-\-threads 8 \-\-gpu\-pct 0
.EE
.RE
